<title>SINGAPORE: Keppel leaps on bank purchase news.</title>
<headline>Keppel leaps on bank purchase news.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Keppel Corp leapt Singapore 15 cents to hit S$6.45 early Friday on news the diversified conglomerate had bought a Philippines bank.</p>
<p>Volume was active with over 1.5 million shares traded by 0115 GMT.  </p>
<p>On Thursday, a Philippine central bank official said Keppel had won control of troubled Monte de Peidad, the oldest savings bank in the Philippines.</p>
<p>Analysts generally welcomed news of Keppel's purchase of the ailing Manila bank as part of the corporation's regional diversification efforts.</p>
<p>-- Angela Tan, Singapore newsroom (65 8703083)</p>
</text>
